course: dictionary
lesson: 13234
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word gemma is a good example. «Gemma waved from the school gate.» Here Gemma is a girl's name, because it has a capital letter and it is a person.
explain: Now read this: «The gemmae were washed out of their little cups by the rain.» There is no girl here. Gemmae is the science word for tiny buds on mosses and liverworts. Those buds break off and grow into new plants, so the context shows you the meaning.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: who or what is this sentence about? If it is about a person, Gemma is a name. If it is about moss, rain or plants, gemma is a tiny bud that can grow into a new plant. Then check by putting your meaning back into the sentence.
fact: Gemma is a girl's name, popular in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: The name Gemma comes from Italian and Latin, and it means «gem» or «jewel».
fact: A gemma is a tiny bud or group of cells on mosses and liverworts.
fact: A gemma breaks off and grows into a new plant, so it is a way for a plant to make copies of itself without seeds or spores.
fact: Gemma is also the name of an AI model made by a technology company.
exercise: «Gemma gave her friend a big hug at the gate.» Who or what is Gemma in this sentence? | A kind of cloud | *A girl's name, because Gemma is a person | A town in the rain | A dog that barks at the gate
exercise: «The raindrops splashed into the little cups on the liverwort.» In a science lesson, what is a gemma? | *A tiny bud on a moss or liverwort that can grow into a new plant | A large stone on a river bed | A bird's egg hidden in a nest
exercise: «Gemma and her brother looked at the moss under the microscope.» Find and copy one word that is a name. | microscope | moss | looked | *Gemma
test: «The gemmae were washed out of the cup and began to grow.» What does gemmae mean here? | A girl's name, used in the plural | *Tiny buds that can grow into new plants | Small stones for a garden path | A kind of raincoat
test: «Gemma is my best friend, and she lives next door.» What does Gemma mean? | A type of garden tool | A rainy day | *A girl's name | Tiny buds on a liverwort
exam: How can you tell which meaning of gemma a text uses? | Gemma always means a tiny bud, so the context does not matter | *Look at the context: a person means the name, while moss, rain or plants mean the science word | Ask the nearest adult and guess | Gemma always means the name, so you never need to check
